{
  "_comment": [
    "GOLDEN CROSS-RUNTIME FIXTURE. Read by BOTH runtimes and diffed byte-for-byte:",
    "  JS      cli/src/peek/derive.js  deriveRow / foldRows, reconcile.js fold",
    "  Python  gateway/app/store.py    derive_row / fold_rows / fold",
    "by gateway/tests/test_store_parity.py. A divergence FAILS the suite; it does not",
    "warn. Two readers of the same append-only log that disagree produce double-counting",
    "that looks exactly like the three prior mispricing incidents.",
    "",
    "Coverage, deliberately: a promotional-window row on both sides of 2026-08-31; an",
    "unpriceable served model; an unpriceable baseline; a non-2xx row; an elig:false row;",
    "a NEGATIVE delta (claude-fable-5 served against claude-opus-5); a cache-heavy row; a",
    "long-context row (>200k input); a speed:'fast' row; a svc:'batch' row; a svc:",
    "'priority' row; an undated row; a row with no baseline; a duplicate STRONG id; a",
    "weak-key pair; a weak-key `served` disagreement; a pre-migration gateway row; a",
    "same-strong-key >2x output outlier; an unknown-TTL cache-create row.",
    "",
    "ONE constraint on new rows: never set BOTH `c5` and `cu` non-zero in the same row.",
    "JS applyRates() prices them as two separate terms at the same cacheWrite rate while",
    "Python's cost_of_model takes one combined argument, so a+b vs (a+b) can differ by one",
    "ulp. With either term zero the addition is exact and the two runtimes agree to the",
    "last bit. Real emitters may set both; the ulp is immaterial to money but fatal to a",
    "byte-identical assertion."
  ],
